From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 05:00:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: Codex installs with its own installer; an update is run
 by Codex itself

Codex was installed and updated with `npm install -g` through whatever npm
the machine had. A machine without Node could not install it at all, and an
installation npm had no right to replace failed with EACCES.

On macOS and Linux, Install now runs Codex's own installer without
questions, through the curl found on the host, and runs nothing when the
download breaks off. It is refused with a reason where it could not give a
working Codex: no curl, a relative CODEX_HOME, or a copy that does not
answer `--version` and lies where the installer does not write.

Update runs `update` of the very copy whose version was read, by its full
path: Codex knows how it was installed and updates itself that way. The
subcommand exists since Codex 0.126.0; an older copy is left to a manual
update. A copy that does not answer `--version` counts as not installed.
Windows keeps bb's npm commands.
